/* ===========================================================================
   osa_qsp_model.dot
   Osteosarcoma (OSA) — mechanistic QSP map
   골육종 (OSA) 기계론적 QSP 지도

   ORGANISING THESIS (see README.md; every number below is computed in
   osa_reference_model.py and printed in osa_reference_output.txt):

     Cure in osteosarcoma is a POISSON BET ON LESIONS NOBODY CAN SEE, and it
     is paid for out of an EXPOSURE BUDGET with three hard organ ceilings.

         P(cure) = exp( -lambda0 * [ 1 - exp( -n0 * e^-K ) ] )
                    \________/       \_______________________/
                     how many          did THIS lesion die
                     lesions           (n0 ~ 1e6 clonogens)

         K = kill integral, subject to
               E_DOX  <= heart,  E_CIS <= cochlea + tubule,
               E_MTX  <= tubule

     lambda0 = 1.80 is fixed by ONE historical number: cure after amputation
     alone is exp(-lambda0) = 0.165, and the reported figure is 0.15-0.20.
     Everything else follows.  To reach the 0.60 that MAP achieves, K must be
     6.6 log10 — and the model delivers 6.61.

     The structure has one more twist that makes the whole regimen strange:
     METHOTREXATE IS CLEARED THROUGH THE ORGAN IT DESTROYS.  86% of the dose
     leaves by the kidney, and the tubular concentration is

         C_tub  =  CL_ren(KID) * C_plasma / UrineFlow(KID)
         S(pH)  =  0.86 * 10^(0.682*(pH-5))  mM      [solubility]

     Everything above S crystallises, obstructs, and lowers BOTH CL_ren and
     UrineFlow — which raises C_tub.  Positive feedback, hence a critical
     urine pH rather than a risk factor.

   SEVEN CONSEQUENCES, ALL ARITHMETIC RATHER THAN ASSERTED:

     A. A BIFURCATION, NOT A GUIDELINE.  Tubular fluid first supersaturates
        at urine pH 7.30, elimination becomes delayed below 7.15, and the
        course causes AKI below 6.95.  The protocol instruction "alkalinise
        to pH >= 7.0, hydrate at 3 L/m2/day" is where this loop changes
        sign — and pH 7.0 sits 0.30 units INSIDE the unstable region, which
        is why delayed elimination still happens under full compliance and
        why the escalation on a rising creatinine is more bicarbonate, not
        less methotrexate.

     B. ONE pH UNIT IS WORTH 4.81x THE FLUID.  C_tub scales as
        dose/urine-flow while S scales as 10^(0.682*pH), so any factor f on
        C_tub is worth log10(f)/0.682 pH units.  Doubling the hydration and
        halving the dose are both worth 0.44 pH units; alkalinisation from
        6.6 to 7.3 does what quadrupling the fluid does.  Arithmetically the
        largest single lever on this regimen's safety is not the dose.

     C. THE LOOP GAIN RISES AS THE KIDNEY FALLS.  Halving the starting GFR
        multiplies the same course's AUC by 1.59x and C48 by 3.8x, and leaves
        the kidney at 53.7% instead of 62.9%.  Twelve methotrexate courses and
        four cisplatin courses are therefore not additive nephrotoxins — they
        are multiplicative through one shared state variable, so course n
        rewrites the pharmacokinetics of courses n+1..12.

     D. THE RESCUE IS DIAGNOSTICALLY GATED TO ARRIVE AFTER THE EXPOSURE IT
        WOULD PREVENT.  Glucarpidase is triggered by a 48-h or 72-h
        concentration, but the AUC is front-loaded: rescue at 12 h removes
        29% of the exposure, at 24 h 10%, at the standard 48-h trigger 2%, and
        at 72 h nothing at all — and end-of-course GFR is unchanged whichever
        you pick.  Nothing rescues the tubule retrospectively.

     E. NECROSIS IS PROGNOSTIC AND MANIPULABLE AT THE SAME TIME.  Huvos
        necrosis and micrometastatic log-kill are two integrals of the same
        sensitivity parameter (r = 0.97), which is why necrosis is the
        strongest prognostic factor in the disease.  But necrosis integrates
        over the PRIMARY, where drug penetration and matrix TGF-beta apply,
        and cure integrates over the LUNG, where they do not — so re-timing
        the same total drug moves the marker without moving the patient.  A
        marker that is prognostic but manipulable is the wrong thing to build
        a treatment decision on, and response-adapted escalation does exactly
        that.

     F. MAPIE'S NULL RESULT IS THE ARITHMETIC OF ITS DESIGN.  Every kill term
        carries the factor (1 - RES).  A "poor responder" is by definition a
        patient in whom that factor is small, so the escalation was tested in
        precisely the subgroup where extra cytotoxic is worth least; and it
        had to buy its five ifosfamide/etoposide cycles by giving up one
        doxorubicin and one cisplatin cycle from a budget already at its
        walls.  Predicted EFS HR 0.98 in poor responders and 0.86 in good
        responders (who were never randomised).  EURAMOS-1: 0.98 (0.78-1.23).

     G. THREE PLATEAU MECHANISMS, NONE OF THEM THE DRUGS.

        (i) DETECTABILITY.  At the real between-patient CV of achieved log-kill
        (25%), a realistic +0.2 log intensification is worth +4 points of cure
        and needs 2764 patients per arm; EURAMOS-1 randomised 618.  The same
        half-log is worth +19.6 points at CV 2% and +3.5 at CV 65% — a 5.5-fold
        difference produced entirely by the spread and not at all by the drug.
        Nothing has ever randomised the spread.

        (ii) INDIFFERENCE.  Under-hydration BUYS +0.4 log10 of kill through
        delayed elimination and pays for it with 12% treatment-related
        mortality, giving survival 0.595 against MAP's 0.596.  The regimen sits
        on an indifference curve, so moves along it read as null however large
        they are.  Only dexrazoxane MOVES the wall: doxorubicin 600 mg/m2 with
        it is the best arm in the whole set (survival 0.649, HR 0.83).

        (iii) THE WRONG RECIPIENT — NOT THE MEAN AND NOT THE TAIL, THE
        SHOULDER.  P(cure) saturates at BOTH ends, so the same total extra
        log-kill is worth +0.116 given to the SECOND quartile of achieved
        exposure, +0.048 spread over everyone, and only +0.030 given to the
        worst quartile.  The marginal value peaks at 6.2-6.6 log10 of achieved
        kill and is zero in the bottom two and top two deciles.  Since necrosis
        tracks achieved log-kill at r = 0.97 the marker CAN find that band — the
        near-misses at roughly 85-89% necrosis.  EURAMOS-1 used the marker
        correctly as a prognostic tool and then spent its escalation budget on
        the group the marker had identified as LEAST salvageable.

   RENDER:
     dot -Tsvg osa_qsp_model.dot -o osa_qsp_model.svg
     dot -Tpng -Gdpi=150 osa_qsp_model.dot -o osa_qsp_model.png
   =========================================================================== */

digraph osteosarcoma_qsp {
    rankdir = TB;
    compound = true;
    newrank = true;
    splines = spline;
    concentrate = false;
    nodesep = 0.22;
    ranksep = 0.48;
    fontname = "Helvetica";
    labelloc = "t";
    labeljust = "l";
    label = <<b>Osteosarcoma — Quantitative Systems Pharmacology Map</b><br/>
<font point-size="13">골육종 QSP 기계론적 지도 · MAP backbone (methotrexate · doxorubicin · cisplatin) + IE · bone-directed · immune · anti-angiogenic</font><br/>
<font point-size="12">P(cure) = exp(−λ₀·[1 − exp(−n₀·e<sup>−K</sup>)]) &nbsp;·&nbsp; λ₀ = 1.80 occult lesions &nbsp;·&nbsp; K bounded by kidney / heart / cochlea</font><br/>
<font point-size="12">Methotrexate is cleared through the organ it destroys: C_tub = CL_ren(KID)·C_p / UF(KID) &nbsp;vs&nbsp; S(pH) = 0.86·10<sup>0.682(pH−5)</sup> mM &nbsp;→&nbsp; critical urine pH 7.30</font>>;
    fontsize = 20;

    node [shape = box, style = "rounded,filled", fontname = "Helvetica",
          fontsize = 10, penwidth = 1.0, margin = "0.07,0.04"];
    edge [fontname = "Helvetica", fontsize = 8, arrowsize = 0.6,
          penwidth = 0.9, color = "#5a5a5a"];

    /* ===================================================================
       1. GENOMICS AND CELL OF ORIGIN
       =================================================================== */
    subgraph cluster_genome {
        label = "① 유전체 불안정성 · 기원세포 (Genomic catastrophe & cell of origin)";
        style = "filled"; color = "#bfa5cf"; fillcolor = "#f4eef8";
        fontsize = 12; fontcolor = "#4a2d5e";
        node [fillcolor = "#e6d8f0", color = "#8e6aa8"];

        TP53      [label = "TP53 loss\n(>90%; Li-Fraumeni)"];
        RB1       [label = "RB1 loss\n(~30%; hereditary Rb)"];
        CHROMO    [label = "Chromothripsis\n(massive rearrangement)"];
        KATAEGIS  [label = "Kataegis\n(localised hypermutation)"];
        ANEUPLOID [label = "Aneuploidy ·\ncomplex karyotype"];
        MDM2      [label = "MDM2 amplification"];
        CDK4      [label = "CDK4 / CCNE1\namplification"];
        MYC       [label = "MYC 8q24 gain"];
        ALT       [label = "ALT / telomere\nmaintenance"];
        RECQL4    [label = "RECQL4\n(Rothmund–Thomson)"];
        PAGET_2   [label = "Paget's disease ·\nprior radiation\n(secondary OS)"];
        MSC       [label = "Osteoblastic\nmesenchymal progenitor\n(cell of origin)"];
        GROWTH_SP [label = "Adolescent growth spurt\n(metaphyseal proliferation)"];
        HRD       [label = "Homologous-recombination\ndeficiency (BRCAness)"];
        CGAS      [label = "cGAS–STING\n(cytosolic dsDNA)"];

        TP53 -> CHROMO; TP53 -> ANEUPLOID; RB1 -> ANEUPLOID;
        CHROMO -> KATAEGIS; CHROMO -> MDM2; CHROMO -> CDK4; CHROMO -> MYC;
        RECQL4 -> CHROMO; PAGET_2 -> CHROMO; ANEUPLOID -> ALT;
        CHROMO -> HRD; ANEUPLOID -> CGAS;
        GROWTH_SP -> MSC; MSC -> ANEUPLOID;
    }

    /* ===================================================================
       2. TUMOUR CELL PROGRAM
       =================================================================== */
    subgraph cluster_tumour {
        label = "② 종양세포 프로그램 (Tumour-cell program & osteoid production)";
        style = "filled"; color = "#c9a37e"; fillcolor = "#fbf3ea";
        fontsize = 12; fontcolor = "#6a4520";
        node [fillcolor = "#f0dcc4", color = "#a97b4a"];

        RUNX2     [label = "RUNX2\n(master osteoblast TF)"];
        SP7       [label = "SP7 / osterix"];
        WNT       [label = "Wnt / β-catenin"];
        NOTCH     [label = "Notch (HES1)"];
        HH        [label = "Hedgehog / GLI"];
        IGF1R     [label = "IGF-1R → PI3K/AKT/mTOR"];
        PRIM      [label = "PRIM\nviable primary tumour\n(mL; ~150 at diagnosis)",
                   shape = box3d, fillcolor = "#e0b681"];
        OSTEOID   [label = "Immature osteoid ·\nmineralisation\n(why volume does not shrink)"];
        NEC       [label = "NEC\nnecrotic tumour volume\n(what the pathologist counts)",
                   shape = box3d, fillcolor = "#e0b681"];
        RES       [label = "RES\nresistant clone fraction\n(ABCB1 · ABCC2 · RFC loss)",
                   shape = box3d, fillcolor = "#d99b5c"];
        PROLIF    [label = "Proliferating fraction"];
        QUIES     [label = "Quiescent / hypoxic\nsanctuary"];
        ALPB      [label = "Serum ALP ↑\n(biomarker)", shape = ellipse,
                   fillcolor = "#fff3d8"];
        LDHB      [label = "Serum LDH ↑\n(biomarker)", shape = ellipse,
                   fillcolor = "#fff3d8"];

        RUNX2 -> SP7 -> OSTEOID; WNT -> RUNX2; NOTCH -> PROLIF; HH -> PROLIF;
        IGF1R -> PROLIF; PROLIF -> PRIM; OSTEOID -> PRIM;
        PRIM -> ALPB; PRIM -> LDHB; PRIM -> QUIES;
        PRIM -> NEC [label = "kill", style = dashed];
        PRIM -> RES [label = "selection", style = dashed];
    }
    MSC -> RUNX2; MYC -> PROLIF; CDK4 -> PROLIF; MDM2 -> PROLIF;

    /* ===================================================================
       3. BONE REMODELLING VICIOUS CYCLE
       =================================================================== */
    subgraph cluster_bone {
        label = "③ 골 재형성 악순환 (The vicious cycle — a GROWTH term, not a SURVIVAL term)";
        style = "filled"; color = "#9fb8d0"; fillcolor = "#eef4f9";
        fontsize = 12; fontcolor = "#254a6b";
        node [fillcolor = "#d6e5f2", color = "#5d87ad"];

        RANKL     [label = "RANKL (TNFSF11)\ntumour-derived"];
        OPG       [label = "OPG (TNFRSF11B)\ndecoy receptor"];
        RANK      [label = "RANK on\nosteoclast precursor"];
        MCSF      [label = "M-CSF / CSF1R"];
        OCL       [label = "OCL\nosteoclast activity",
                   shape = box3d, fillcolor = "#b9d2e8"];
        CTSK      [label = "Cathepsin K · TRAP ·\nH⁺-ATPase"];
        RESORB    [label = "Resorption lacuna ·\nosteolysis"];
        TGFM      [label = "TGFM\nmatrix-liberated\nTGF-β / IGF-1 / BMP-2",
                   shape = box3d, fillcolor = "#b9d2e8"];
        PTHRP     [label = "PTHrP"];
        IL6_11    [label = "IL-6 · IL-11"];
        OBL       [label = "Osteoblast\n(aberrant new bone)"];
        SCLERO    [label = "Sclerostin · DKK1"];
        FRACTURE  [label = "Pathologic fracture ·\nCodman triangle ·\nsunburst periostitis",
                   shape = ellipse, fillcolor = "#fde8e8"];
        BONEPAIN  [label = "Bone pain (VAS)",
                   shape = ellipse, fillcolor = "#fde8e8"];

        RANKL -> RANK; OPG -> RANKL [label = "sequesters", arrowhead = tee];
        MCSF -> RANK; RANK -> OCL -> CTSK -> RESORB -> TGFM;
        PTHRP -> RANKL; IL6_11 -> RANKL; OCL -> OBL; SCLERO -> OBL [arrowhead = tee];
        RESORB -> FRACTURE; RESORB -> BONEPAIN; OBL -> FRACTURE;
    }
    PRIM -> RANKL [label = "tumour burden"]; PRIM -> PTHRP; PRIM -> IL6_11;
    TGFM -> PROLIF [label = "×(1+0.45·TGFM)\nGROWTH only", color = "#b03030",
                    fontcolor = "#b03030", penwidth = 1.4];
    OCL -> ALPB;

    /* ===================================================================
       4. TUMOUR MICROENVIRONMENT AND IMMUNITY
       =================================================================== */
    subgraph cluster_immune {
        label = "④ 종양 미세환경 · 면역 (Immune microenvironment — the only compartment mifamurtide touches)";
        style = "filled"; color = "#8fc4a8"; fillcolor = "#eef8f2";
        fontsize = 12; fontcolor = "#1f5c3d";
        node [fillcolor = "#d2ecdd", color = "#4e9b73"];

        TAM_M1    [label = "M1 tumour-associated\nmacrophage"];
        M2        [label = "M2 / TAM\nimmunosuppressive",
                   shape = box3d, fillcolor = "#b5dfc6"];
        CTL       [label = "CTL\nCD8⁺ cytotoxic T cell",
                   shape = box3d, fillcolor = "#b5dfc6"];
        TREG      [label = "Treg (FOXP3⁺)"];
        MDSC      [label = "MDSC"];
        NK        [label = "NK cell"];
        PDL1      [label = "PD-L1 / PD-1 axis\n(low TMB → checkpoint failure)"];
        IFNG      [label = "IFN-γ"];
        TGFB_I    [label = "TGF-β · IL-10\n(immune brake)"];
        ALVMAC    [label = "Pulmonary ALVEOLAR\nmacrophage\n(the lung is where cure lives)"];
        NOD2      [label = "NOD2 receptor\n(muramyl tripeptide sensor)"];
        TNFA      [label = "TNF-α · IL-1β · IL-6"];
        KILLIMM   [label = "km_imm\nimmune clearance of\nlung micrometastases\n(×LUNG_IMM = 4)",
                   shape = box3d, fillcolor = "#9fd4b4"];

        TAM_M1 -> IFNG -> CTL; M2 -> TGFB_I -> CTL [arrowhead = tee];
        TREG -> CTL [arrowhead = tee]; MDSC -> CTL [arrowhead = tee];
        M2 -> PDL1; PDL1 -> CTL [arrowhead = tee];
        NOD2 -> ALVMAC -> TNFA; ALVMAC -> KILLIMM; CTL -> KILLIMM; NK -> KILLIMM;
        M2 -> KILLIMM [arrowhead = tee];
    }
    CGAS -> IFNG [style = dashed]; ANEUPLOID -> PDL1 [style = dashed];

    /* ===================================================================
       5. ANGIOGENESIS, HYPOXIA AND DRUG PENETRATION
       =================================================================== */
    subgraph cluster_vasc {
        label = "⑤ 혈관신생 · 저산소 · 약물 침투 (Angiogenesis, hypoxia and the penetration penalty)";
        style = "filled"; color = "#d69f9f"; fillcolor = "#fbeeee";
        fontsize = 12; fontcolor = "#6e2a2a";
        node [fillcolor = "#f3d6d6", color = "#b06a6a"];

        HIF1A     [label = "HIF-1α"];
        VEGFA     [label = "VEGF-A"];
        PDGFB     [label = "PDGF-B · FGF-2 ·\nANGPT2"];
        VEGFR2    [label = "VEGFR2 / KDR"];
        VASC      [label = "VASC\nfunctional vascular density",
                   shape = box3d, fillcolor = "#eec4c4"];
        HYP       [label = "HYP\nhypoxic fraction",
                   shape = box3d, fillcolor = "#eec4c4"];
        IFP       [label = "Interstitial fluid\npressure ↑ · mineralised matrix"];
        PEN       [label = "PEN\ndrug penetration factor\n0.30 + 0.70·VASC/(VASC+0.55)",
                   shape = box3d, fillcolor = "#e5a9a9"];

        HIF1A -> VEGFA -> VEGFR2 -> VASC; PDGFB -> VASC;
        VASC -> HYP [arrowhead = tee]; HYP -> HIF1A;
        VASC -> PEN; IFP -> PEN [arrowhead = tee]; HYP -> QUIES;
    }
    PRIM -> VEGFA; PRIM -> IFP;
    PEN -> PRIM [label = "primary only:\nmicromets are fully perfused",
                 style = dashed, color = "#b03030", fontcolor = "#b03030"];

    /* ===================================================================
       6. THE METASTATIC CASCADE — WHERE CURE IS DECIDED
       =================================================================== */
    subgraph cluster_met {
        label = "⑥ 전이 캐스케이드 · 포아송 구조 (The metastatic cascade — a Poisson bet on lesions nobody can see)";
        style = "filled"; color = "#8f8fc4"; fillcolor = "#eeeef8";
        fontsize = 12; fontcolor = "#2d2d6b";
        node [fillcolor = "#d8d8f0", color = "#6a6aa8"];

        EMT       [label = "EMT · SNAI2 · TWIST1"];
        EZRIN     [label = "Ezrin (VIL2)\nmembrane–cytoskeleton link"];
        CXCR4     [label = "CXCR4 / CXCL12 axis"];
        MMP       [label = "MMP-2 · MMP-9 ·\nMT1-MMP"];
        INTRA     [label = "Intravasation\n(thin-walled sinusoids)"];
        CTC       [label = "Circulating tumour cell ·\nplatelet cloaking"];
        LUNGARR   [label = "Pulmonary capillary arrest\n(first-pass organ)"];
        DORMANT   [label = "Dormancy\n(angiogenesis-limited;\nKGM ≈ 0.35·KG)"];
        LMET      [label = "LMET\nln(clonogens per lesion)\nstarts at ln(1e6) = 13.8",
                   shape = box3d, fillcolor = "#c4c4e8"];
        LAMBDA0   [label = "λ₀ = 1.80\noccult lesions at diagnosis\n(Poisson)",
                   shape = doubleoctagon, fillcolor = "#b3b3e0"];
        SURGALONE [label = "exp(−λ₀) = 0.165\ncure after amputation alone\n= THE CALIBRATION ANCHOR",
                   shape = note, fillcolor = "#fff2c9", color = "#b08a20"];
        KINT      [label = "K = 13.8 − LMET\nmicrometastatic log-kill\nMAP delivers 6.61 log10",
                   shape = box3d, fillcolor = "#a8a8dc"];
        CURE      [label = "P(cure) = exp(−λ₀·[1−exp(−n₀e^−K)])\nDOUBLE exponential in exposure",
                   shape = doubleoctagon, fillcolor = "#9a9ad4"];
        LUNGMET   [label = "Radiographic lung\nmetastases (RECIST) ·\nmetastasectomy",
                   shape = ellipse, fillcolor = "#fde8e8"];
        SKIPMET   [label = "Skip metastasis ·\nbone-to-bone spread",
                   shape = ellipse, fillcolor = "#fde8e8"];

        EMT -> INTRA; EZRIN -> LUNGARR; CXCR4 -> LUNGARR; MMP -> INTRA;
        INTRA -> CTC -> LUNGARR -> DORMANT -> LMET;
        LAMBDA0 -> CURE; LAMBDA0 -> SURGALONE; LMET -> KINT -> CURE;
        DORMANT -> LUNGMET; CTC -> SKIPMET;
    }
    PRIM -> EMT; PRIM -> MMP; HYP -> EMT; TGFM -> EMT;
    KILLIMM -> KINT [label = "the only immune\nterm that counts",
                     color = "#1f7a4d", fontcolor = "#1f7a4d", penwidth = 1.3];

    /* ===================================================================
       7. METHOTREXATE PK AND THE RENAL FEEDBACK LOOP
       =================================================================== */
    subgraph cluster_mtx {
        label = "⑦ 고용량 메토트렉세이트 PK · 신장 양성 피드백 루프 (HDMTX 12 g/m² — the drug is cleared through the organ it destroys)";
        style = "filled"; color = "#d8b44a"; fillcolor = "#fdf8e6";
        fontsize = 12; fontcolor = "#6b5410";
        node [fillcolor = "#faedbe", color = "#b3902c"];

        MTXDOSE   [label = "HDMTX 12 g/m²\n4-h infusion ×12 courses",
                   shape = invhouse, fillcolor = "#f2dc8e"];
        A1        [label = "A1 central\nV1 = 18 L\nC_max ≈ 890 µM",
                   shape = box3d, fillcolor = "#f5e3a3"];
        A2        [label = "A2 peripheral\nV2 = 10 L"];
        A3        [label = "A3 deep / third space\nV3 = 5 L (effusion, ascites)"];
        CL_NR     [label = "Non-renal CL 1.2 L/h\n(7-OH-MTX, biliary,\nenterohepatic recycling)"];
        RFC       [label = "SLC19A1 / RFC influx ·\nFPGS polyglutamation"];
        ABC_MTX   [label = "ABCC2 · ABCG2 efflux"];
        MPGT      [label = "MPGT\nMTX-polyglutamate,\ntumour",
                   shape = box3d, fillcolor = "#f5e3a3"];
        MPGM      [label = "MPGM\nMTX-polyglutamate,\nmarrow & mucosa",
                   shape = box3d, fillcolor = "#f5e3a3"];
        DHFR      [label = "DHFR inhibition"];
        TS        [label = "Thymidylate synthase ·\nGART / AICAR block"];
        DTMP      [label = "dUMP → dTMP block ·\nthymineless death"];
        MTHFR     [label = "MTHFR C677T\n(pharmacogenetic)"];

        GFR       [label = "GFR = 7.2 L/h × KID"];
        CLREN     [label = "CL_ren = 7.5 L/h × KID\n× (1 − 0.85·OBS)\n86% of total clearance",
                   fillcolor = "#f2dc8e"];
        UF        [label = "Urine flow UF\n0.21 L/h at 3 L/m²/day\n× KID × (1 − 0.90·OBS)"];
        CTUB      [label = "C_tub = CL_ren·C_p / UF\n≈ 32 mM at peak",
                   shape = box3d, fillcolor = "#efd478"];
        URINEPH   [label = "URINE pH\n(bicarbonate / acetazolamide)",
                   shape = invhouse, fillcolor = "#f2dc8e"];
        SOL       [label = "S(pH) = 0.86·10^{0.682(pH−5)} mM\n0.86 / 4.14 / 19.9 / 43.6\nat pH 5 / 6 / 7 / 7.5",
                   shape = note, fillcolor = "#fff2c9", color = "#b08a20"];
        PPT       [label = "PPT\ntubular crystal burden",
                   shape = box3d, fillcolor = "#efd478"];
        OBS       [label = "OBS = PPT/(PPT+2)\nintratubular obstruction"];
        KID       [label = "KID\nkidney functional mass\n(the SHARED state variable)",
                   shape = box3d, fillcolor = "#e8c455", penwidth = 1.6];
        CRITPH    [label = "CRITICAL URINE pH\nsupersaturation 7.30\ndelayed elimination 7.15\nAKI 6.95",
                   shape = doubleoctagon, fillcolor = "#f0c03c", color = "#8a6a10"];
        EXCH      [label = "1 pH unit = 4.81× the fluid\n= a 4.81-fold dose cut\n(log10 f / 0.682)",
                   shape = note, fillcolor = "#fff2c9", color = "#b08a20"];

        MTXDOSE -> A1; A1 -> A2 [dir = both]; A1 -> A3 [dir = both];
        A1 -> CL_NR; A1 -> RFC -> MPGT; A1 -> MPGM; ABC_MTX -> MPGT [arrowhead = tee];
        MPGT -> DHFR -> TS -> DTMP; MTHFR -> TS;
        A1 -> CLREN -> CTUB; GFR -> CLREN; UF -> CTUB [arrowhead = tee];
        URINEPH -> SOL; SOL -> PPT [arrowhead = tee];
        CTUB -> PPT [label = "excess above S"];
        PPT -> OBS; OBS -> CLREN [arrowhead = tee, color = "#b03030", penwidth = 1.5];
        OBS -> UF [arrowhead = tee, color = "#b03030", penwidth = 1.5];
        PPT -> KID [arrowhead = tee, color = "#b03030", penwidth = 1.5];
        CTUB -> KID [label = "direct tubular\ntoxicity", arrowhead = tee,
                     color = "#b03030"];
        KID -> GFR; KID -> CLREN; KID -> UF;
        SOL -> CRITPH; CTUB -> CRITPH; SOL -> EXCH;
    }
    /* the loop, drawn as a loop */
    KID -> CTUB [label = "  ⟲ POSITIVE FEEDBACK\n  injury → less clearance & less flow\n  → higher C_tub → more crystal",
                 color = "#c00000", fontcolor = "#c00000", penwidth = 2.2,
                 style = bold, constraint = false];

    /* ===================================================================
       8. LEUCOVORIN RESCUE AND GLUCARPIDASE
       =================================================================== */
    subgraph cluster_rescue {
        label = "⑧ 류코보린 구조요법 · 글루카르피다제 (Rescue — a shared clock, and a rescue that arrives too late)";
        style = "filled"; color = "#a8cf7e"; fillcolor = "#f4f9ec";
        fontsize = 12; fontcolor = "#40621b";
        node [fillcolor = "#e0efc9", color = "#7ba348"];

        LV        [label = "Leucovorin 15 mg/m² q6h\nfrom +24 h × 48 h",
                   shape = invhouse, fillcolor = "#d2e8b0"];
        RFT       [label = "RFT\nreduced folate, tumour",
                   shape = box3d, fillcolor = "#d2e8b0"];
        RFM       [label = "RFM\nreduced folate, marrow\n(taken up 2.75× faster)",
                   shape = box3d, fillcolor = "#d2e8b0"];
        KIAPP     [label = "Apparent Ki = 1.10·(1 + RF/0.60)\nrescue RAISES the Ki\nin BOTH compartments"];
        SHAREDCLK [label = "THE SHARED CLOCK\nrescue timing sets the\ntherapeutic window, and it\nrescues the tumour too",
                   shape = note, fillcolor = "#fff2c9", color = "#b08a20"];
        TDM       [label = "TDM: C24 < 10 µM,\nC48 < 1 µM, C72 < 0.1 µM\n(model: 8.8 / 0.56 / 0.04)",
                   shape = ellipse, fillcolor = "#e8f4d8"];
        GLUC      [label = "Glucarpidase 50 U/kg\n(carboxypeptidase G2)",
                   shape = invhouse, fillcolor = "#d2e8b0"];
        DAMPA     [label = "MTX → DAMPA + glutamate\n(adds ~90 L/h of CL)"];
        LATE      [label = "TRIGGERED BY A 48-h VALUE\nremoves 11% of AUC at 24 h,\n2% at 48 h, <1% at 72 h,\nand 0 of the tubular injury",
                   shape = doubleoctagon, fillcolor = "#f0c03c", color = "#8a6a10"];

        LV -> RFT; LV -> RFM; RFT -> KIAPP; RFM -> KIAPP;
        KIAPP -> SHAREDCLK; GLUC -> DAMPA; DAMPA -> LATE; TDM -> GLUC;
    }
    A1 -> TDM; RFT -> MPGT [arrowhead = tee, label = "competes"];
    RFM -> MPGM [arrowhead = tee]; DAMPA -> A1 [arrowhead = tee];
    KIAPP -> DTMP [arrowhead = tee];

    /* ===================================================================
       9. DOXORUBICIN AND THE CARDIAC CEILING
       =================================================================== */
    subgraph cluster_dox {
        label = "⑨ 독소루비신 · 심장 천장 (Doxorubicin — the ceiling dexrazoxane can actually move)";
        style = "filled"; color = "#cf7ea8"; fillcolor = "#fbeef4";
        fontsize = 12; fontcolor = "#6b1f45";
        node [fillcolor = "#f2d0e2", color = "#a8497b"];

        DOXDOSE   [label = "Doxorubicin 75 mg/m²\n48-h infusion ×6\n= 450 mg/m² cumulative",
                   shape = invhouse, fillcolor = "#e8b3cf"];
        DOXC      [label = "DOXC central\nV = 25 L, CL = 45 L/h",
                   shape = box3d, fillcolor = "#eec2d8"];
        DOXP      [label = "DOXP peripheral\nV = 1200 L (deep tissue)"];
        TOP2A     [label = "TOP2A poisoning\n→ DNA double-strand breaks"];
        ROS_T     [label = "Redox cycling · ROS ·\nDNA intercalation"];
        ABCB1     [label = "ABCB1 / P-gp efflux"];
        CBR1      [label = "CBR1 / AKR1A1\n(carbonyl reduction)"];
        DOXOL     [label = "DOXOL\ndoxorubicinol\n(the cardiotoxic metabolite)",
                   shape = box3d, fillcolor = "#eec2d8"];
        TOP2B     [label = "TOP2B in cardiomyocyte\n(the actual cardiac target)"];
        FEDOX     [label = "Fe(III)–anthracycline\ncomplex · mitochondrial ROS"];
        CMV       [label = "CMV\ncardiomyocyte viability\n(essentially irreversible)",
                   shape = box3d, fillcolor = "#e8a8c8"];
        DEXR      [label = "Dexrazoxane 10:1\n(iron chelation +\nTOP2B degradation)",
                   shape = invhouse, fillcolor = "#e8b3cf"];
        LVEF      [label = "LVEF\n62.0 → 58.5 after MAP\n→ 59.8 with dexrazoxane",
                   shape = ellipse, fillcolor = "#fde8e8"];
        TROPO     [label = "hs-troponin I ·\nNT-proBNP · GLS",
                   shape = ellipse, fillcolor = "#fde8e8"];
        CARDSTOP  [label = "PROTOCOL STOP RULE\nno more anthracycline\nbelow LVEF 50%",
                   shape = doubleoctagon, fillcolor = "#f0c03c", color = "#8a6a10"];
        LATECARD  [label = "Late cardiomyopathy ·\nheart failure decades on",
                   shape = ellipse, fillcolor = "#fde8e8"];

        DOXDOSE -> DOXC; DOXC -> DOXP [dir = both]; DOXC -> TOP2A; DOXC -> ROS_T;
        ABCB1 -> DOXC [arrowhead = tee]; DOXC -> CBR1 -> DOXOL;
        DOXOL -> TOP2B -> CMV [arrowhead = tee]; DOXOL -> FEDOX -> CMV [arrowhead = tee];
        DEXR -> FEDOX [arrowhead = tee, color = "#1f7a4d", penwidth = 1.6];
        DEXR -> TOP2B [arrowhead = tee, color = "#1f7a4d", penwidth = 1.6];
        CMV -> LVEF -> CARDSTOP; CMV -> TROPO; CMV -> LATECARD;
    }
    TOP2A -> PRIM [arrowhead = tee]; ROS_T -> PRIM [arrowhead = tee];

    /* ===================================================================
       10. CISPLATIN, THE TUBULE AND THE COCHLEA
       =================================================================== */
    subgraph cluster_cis {
        label = "⑩ 시스플라틴 · 세뇨관 · 와우 (Cisplatin — two irreversible ceilings, one of them shared with methotrexate)";
        style = "filled"; color = "#7eb8cf"; fillcolor = "#eef6fb";
        fontsize = 12; fontcolor = "#1f4d63";
        node [fillcolor = "#cee6f2", color = "#4a86a8"];

        CISDOSE   [label = "Cisplatin 120 mg/m²\n72-h infusion ×4\n= 480 mg/m² cumulative",
                   shape = invhouse, fillcolor = "#b0d4e8"];
        CISC      [label = "CISC\nV = 18 L, CL = 30 L/h",
                   shape = box3d, fillcolor = "#c2dcee"];
        AQUA      [label = "Aquation → reactive\nmono/di-aqua species"];
        ADDT      [label = "ADDT\nPt–DNA intrastrand adducts,\ntumour",
                   shape = box3d, fillcolor = "#c2dcee"];
        ERCC1     [label = "ERCC1 / XPF\nnucleotide-excision repair"];
        GSH_MT    [label = "Glutathione ·\nmetallothionein\n(detoxification)"];
        OCT2      [label = "OCT2 / SLC22A2 uptake\ninto proximal tubule"];
        ADDK      [label = "ADDK\nPt adducts, tubule",
                   shape = box3d, fillcolor = "#c2dcee"];
        MG        [label = "Renal Mg²⁺ / K⁺ wasting",
                   shape = ellipse, fillcolor = "#e8f0f8"];
        OCT_COCH  [label = "Cochlear outer hair cell ·\nstria vascularis · TRPV1"];
        ADDC      [label = "ADDC\nPt adducts, cochlea\n(repair t½ ≫ therapy)",
                   shape = box3d, fillcolor = "#c2dcee"];
        HL        [label = "High-frequency hearing loss\n12.2 dB after MAP\n(SIOP / Brock grade)",
                   shape = ellipse, fillcolor = "#fde8e8"];
        STS       [label = "Sodium thiosulfate\n(otoprotection; timing\nvs efficacy trade-off)",
                   shape = invhouse, fillcolor = "#b0d4e8"];
        AMIFOS    [label = "Amifostine · hydration ·\nMg supplementation",
                   shape = invhouse, fillcolor = "#b0d4e8"];

        CISDOSE -> CISC -> AQUA; AQUA -> ADDT; ERCC1 -> ADDT [arrowhead = tee];
        GSH_MT -> AQUA [arrowhead = tee]; CISC -> OCT2 -> ADDK -> MG;
        CISC -> OCT_COCH -> ADDC -> HL; STS -> ADDC [arrowhead = tee];
        AMIFOS -> ADDK [arrowhead = tee];
    }
    ADDT -> PRIM [arrowhead = tee]; ADDT -> KINT [style = dashed];
    ADDK -> KID [arrowhead = tee, color = "#c00000", penwidth = 1.8,
                 label = "  the SHARED ceiling:\n  cisplatin lowers the\n  kidney that methotrexate\n  needs for 11 more courses",
                 fontcolor = "#c00000"];

    /* ===================================================================
       11. IFOSFAMIDE / ETOPOSIDE — THE ESCALATION ARM
       =================================================================== */
    subgraph cluster_ie {
        label = "⑪ 이포스파미드 · 에토포시드 (MAPIE escalation — buys cycles by giving up backbone)";
        style = "filled"; color = "#b0b0b0"; fillcolor = "#f4f4f4";
        fontsize = 12; fontcolor = "#3a3a3a";
        node [fillcolor = "#e2e2e2", color = "#8a8a8a"];

        IFODOSE   [label = "Ifosfamide 2.8 g/m²/d ×5\n×5 cycles (14 g/m²/cycle)",
                   shape = invhouse, fillcolor = "#d0d0d0"];
        CYP3A4    [label = "CYP3A4 / CYP2B6\n4-hydroxylation"];
        IFOA      [label = "IFOA\n4-OH-ifosfamide →\nisophosphoramide mustard",
                   shape = box3d, fillcolor = "#d8d8d8"];
        ACROLEIN  [label = "Acrolein\n(haemorrhagic cystitis)"];
        CAA       [label = "Chloroacetaldehyde\n(neuro- and nephrotoxic)"];
        MESNA     [label = "Mesna",
                   shape = invhouse, fillcolor = "#d0d0d0"];
        ETODOSE   [label = "Etoposide 100 mg/m²/d ×5",
                   shape = invhouse, fillcolor = "#d0d0d0"];
        ETOC      [label = "ETOC\nTOP2 catalytic poison",
                   shape = box3d, fillcolor = "#d8d8d8"];
        SECAML    [label = "Secondary AML / MDS\n(11q23, balanced\ntranslocations)",
                   shape = ellipse, fillcolor = "#fde8e8"];
        FANCONI   [label = "Fanconi syndrome ·\nifosfamide encephalopathy",
                   shape = ellipse, fillcolor = "#fde8e8"];
        TRADEOFF  [label = "THE TRADE, NOT THE ADDITION\n−1 doxorubicin, −1 cisplatin,\n+5 IE cycles, RDI 90%,\ncourses on schedule 76%",
                   shape = doubleoctagon, fillcolor = "#f0c03c", color = "#8a6a10"];

        IFODOSE -> CYP3A4 -> IFOA; IFOA -> ACROLEIN; IFOA -> CAA;
        MESNA -> ACROLEIN [arrowhead = tee]; ACROLEIN -> FANCONI; CAA -> FANCONI;
        ETODOSE -> ETOC -> SECAML; IFOA -> TRADEOFF; ETOC -> TRADEOFF;
    }
    IFOA -> PRIM [arrowhead = tee]; ETOC -> PRIM [arrowhead = tee];
    CAA -> KID [arrowhead = tee, color = "#b03030"];

    /* ===================================================================
       12. BONE-DIRECTED, IMMUNE AND ANTI-ANGIOGENIC AGENTS
       =================================================================== */
    subgraph cluster_other {
        label = "⑫ 골표적 · 면역 · 항혈관 약제 (Bone-directed, immune and anti-angiogenic agents — the negative trials)";
        style = "filled"; color = "#c4b08f"; fillcolor = "#f9f6ee";
        fontsize = 12; fontcolor = "#5a4a20";
        node [fillcolor = "#eae2cc", color = "#a89660"];

        ZOL       [label = "Zoledronate 4 mg q4w\n(OS2006)",
                   shape = invhouse, fillcolor = "#ddd2b0"];
        DENO      [label = "Denosumab 120 mg q4w\n(anti-RANKL mAb)",
                   shape = invhouse, fillcolor = "#ddd2b0"];
        MIFA      [label = "Mifamurtide (L-MTP-PE)\n2 mg/m² 2×/wk → 1×/wk\n(INT-0133)",
                   shape = invhouse, fillcolor = "#ddd2b0"];
        REGO      [label = "Regorafenib · cabozantinib ·\nlenvatinib · apatinib\n(REGOBONE, CABONE)",
                   shape = invhouse, fillcolor = "#ddd2b0"];
        IFNA      [label = "Pegylated interferon α-2b\n(MAPifn arm, EURAMOS-1)",
                   shape = invhouse, fillcolor = "#ddd2b0"];
        CHECKPT   [label = "Pembrolizumab · nivolumab\n(low TMB, cold tumour)",
                   shape = invhouse, fillcolor = "#ddd2b0"];
        GEMDOC    [label = "Gemcitabine/docetaxel ·\nhigh-dose ifosfamide\n(relapse)",
                   shape = invhouse, fillcolor = "#ddd2b0"];
        SAMARIUM  [label = "¹⁵³Sm-EDTMP · ²²³Ra\n(bone-seeking radionuclide)",
                   shape = invhouse, fillcolor = "#ddd2b0"];
        TWOREAD   [label = "TWO READ-OUTS, TWO INTEGRALS\nzoledronate cuts osteoclast\ndrive 25% and ALP 61%,\nand moves log-kill by −0.00",
                   shape = doubleoctagon, fillcolor = "#f0c03c", color = "#8a6a10"];

        ZOL -> TWOREAD; DENO -> TWOREAD;
    }
    ZOL -> OCL [arrowhead = tee, penwidth = 1.3];
    DENO -> RANKL [arrowhead = tee, penwidth = 1.3];
    MIFA -> NOD2 [penwidth = 1.4, color = "#1f7a4d"];
    MIFA -> M2 [arrowhead = tee, color = "#1f7a4d"];
    REGO -> VEGFR2 [arrowhead = tee]; IFNA -> CTL; CHECKPT -> PDL1 [arrowhead = tee];
    GEMDOC -> PRIM [arrowhead = tee]; SAMARIUM -> PRIM [arrowhead = tee];

    /* ===================================================================
       13. TOXICITY GOVERNOR — THE PROTOCOL GO / NO-GO GATES
       =================================================================== */
    subgraph cluster_tox {
        label = "⑬ 독성 · 용량 강도 조절기 (The governor — go/no-go gates are where escalation SPENDS the budget)";
        style = "filled"; color = "#cf9f7e"; fillcolor = "#fbf2ec";
        fontsize = 12; fontcolor = "#6b3a1f";
        node [fillcolor = "#f2ddcc", color = "#a86f49"];

        PROL      [label = "PROL\nproliferating marrow\n(Friberg, MTT 125 h)",
                   shape = box3d, fillcolor = "#eecdb4"];
        TR123     [label = "TR1 → TR2 → TR3\nmaturation transit chain"];
        CIRC      [label = "CIRC\ncirculating ANC\nnadir 0.39 ×10⁹/L on MAP",
                   shape = box3d, fillcolor = "#eecdb4"];
        FBK       [label = "Feedback (CIRC0/CIRC)^0.17 ·\nG-CSF"];
        MUC       [label = "MUC\nmucositis grade 0–4\n(peak 2.1 on MAP)",
                   shape = box3d, fillcolor = "#eecdb4"];
        FN        [label = "Febrile neutropenia ·\nline sepsis",
                   shape = ellipse, fillcolor = "#fde8e8"];
        GATE      [label = "GO / NO-GO GATES\nMTX: ANC ≥ 0.75, MUC < 3, KID ≥ 0.60\nAP: ANC ≥ 1.0 · IE: ANC ≥ 1.0\nDOX: LVEF ≥ 50%",
                   shape = doubleoctagon, fillcolor = "#f0c03c", color = "#8a6a10"];
        DEFER     [label = "Deferral (≤2 wk) at −25% dose\n→ omission beyond that"];
        RDI       [label = "Relative dose intensity\nMAP 100% · MAPIE 90%",
                   shape = ellipse, fillcolor = "#fce8d8"];
        TRM       [label = "TRM\ntreatment-related mortality\n= infection×mucositis + renal\n+ cardiac + baseline",
                   shape = box3d, fillcolor = "#e8b48c"];

        PROL -> TR123 -> CIRC -> FBK -> PROL; CIRC -> FN;
        CIRC -> GATE; MUC -> GATE; GATE -> DEFER -> RDI;
        CIRC -> TRM; MUC -> TRM;
    }
    MPGM -> PROL [arrowhead = tee]; MPGM -> MUC;
    DOXC -> PROL [arrowhead = tee]; CISC -> PROL [arrowhead = tee];
    ETOC -> PROL [arrowhead = tee]; IFOA -> PROL [arrowhead = tee];
    KID -> GATE; KID -> TRM; LVEF -> GATE; CMV -> TRM;
    RDI -> KINT [label = "the budget the\nescalation spends", style = dashed,
                 color = "#c00000", fontcolor = "#c00000"];

    /* ===================================================================
       14. LOCAL CONTROL AND SURGERY
       =================================================================== */
    subgraph cluster_surg {
        label = "⑭ 국소 치료 (Local control — where the primary leaves the model at week 11)";
        style = "filled"; color = "#9f9fcf"; fillcolor = "#f0f0f9";
        fontsize = 12; fontcolor = "#33336b";
        node [fillcolor = "#dcdcf0", color = "#6f6fa8"];

        SURGERY   [label = "Wide en-bloc resection,\nweek 11",
                   shape = invhouse, fillcolor = "#c8c8e8"];
        MARGIN    [label = "Margin status\n(R0 vs R1)"];
        LIMBSALV  [label = "Limb salvage vs amputation ·\nendoprosthesis ·\nrotationplasty",
                   shape = ellipse, fillcolor = "#e8e8f6"];
        HUVOS     [label = "HUVOS NECROSIS %\n= NEC/(NEC+PRIM) at week 11\n≥ 90% = good responder\n(MAP: 90.3%)",
                   shape = doubleoctagon, fillcolor = "#f0c03c", color = "#8a6a10"];
        LOCALREC  [label = "Local recurrence",
                   shape = ellipse, fillcolor = "#fde8e8"];
        MSTS      [label = "MSTS / TESS\nfunctional score",
                   shape = ellipse, fillcolor = "#e8e8f6"];
        RT        [label = "Proton / carbon-ion RT\n(axial, unresectable)",
                   shape = invhouse, fillcolor = "#c8c8e8"];

        SURGERY -> MARGIN -> LOCALREC; SURGERY -> LIMBSALV -> MSTS;
        MARGIN -> HUVOS [style = invis]; RT -> LOCALREC [arrowhead = tee];
    }
    PRIM -> SURGERY; NEC -> HUVOS; PRIM -> HUVOS;
    HUVOS -> KINT [label = "  r = 0.97 — the SAME parameter,\n  read twice; PROGNOSTIC but\n  MANIPULABLE, so it must not\n  drive the treatment decision",
                   style = bold, color = "#c00000", fontcolor = "#c00000",
                   penwidth = 1.8, constraint = false];
    ZOL -> LOCALREC [label = "OS2006:\nworse local control",
                     color = "#b03030", fontcolor = "#b03030"];

    /* ===================================================================
       15. CLINICAL ENDPOINTS
       =================================================================== */
    subgraph cluster_end {
        label = "⑮ 임상 종말점 (Clinical endpoints — read the SURVIVAL column, not the kill column)";
        style = "filled"; color = "#cf7e7e"; fillcolor = "#fdeeee";
        fontsize = 12; fontcolor = "#6b1f1f";
        node [shape = ellipse, fillcolor = "#f8d8d8", color = "#a84949"];

        EFS       [label = "EFS / RFS\n(the randomised endpoint)"];
        OSURV     [label = "OVERALL SURVIVAL\n= cure × (1 − TRM)\nMAP 0.596 · surgery alone 0.168",
                   shape = doubleoctagon, fillcolor = "#f0a0a0", color = "#8a2020"];
        LATEEFF   [label = "Late effects: cardiomyopathy,\nhearing loss, CKD, infertility,\nsecondary malignancy"];
        HRQOL     [label = "HRQoL · growth arrest ·\nlimb-length discrepancy"];
        RELAPSE   [label = "Pulmonary relapse\n(median ~1.5 y)"];
        INDIFF    [label = "THE INDIFFERENCE CURVE\nunder-hydration buys +0.4 log10\nof kill and pays 12% TRM:\nsurvival 0.595 vs 0.596",
                   shape = doubleoctagon, fillcolor = "#f0c03c", color = "#8a6a10"];
        POWER     [label = "THE DETECTABILITY WALL\n+0.2 log = +2 points of survival\n→ 2764 per arm needed;\nEURAMOS-1 randomised 618",
                   shape = doubleoctagon, fillcolor = "#f0c03c", color = "#8a6a10"];
        TAILFIX   [label = "WHAT WOULD WORK\nspend the same total log-kill\non the bottom quartile of\nachieved exposure, not on everyone",
                   shape = note, fillcolor = "#e6f6e6", color = "#2f7a2f"];

        EFS -> OSURV; RELAPSE -> EFS; LATEEFF -> HRQOL;
        INDIFF -> OSURV; POWER -> EFS; TAILFIX -> OSURV;
    }
    CURE -> EFS; CURE -> OSURV; TRM -> OSURV [penwidth = 1.6, color = "#c00000"];
    LMET -> RELAPSE; HL -> LATEEFF; LVEF -> LATEEFF; KID -> LATEEFF;
    SECAML -> LATEEFF; LOCALREC -> EFS; LUNGMET -> EFS;
    HUVOS -> EFS [label = "prognostic", style = dashed];
    RDI -> POWER [style = dashed]; TRM -> INDIFF [style = dashed];

    /* ===================================================================
       LEGEND
       =================================================================== */
    subgraph cluster_legend {
        label = "범례 (Legend)";
        style = "filled"; color = "#9a9a9a"; fillcolor = "#fafafa";
        fontsize = 12; fontcolor = "#333333";
        node [fontsize = 9];

        L1 [label = "ODE state variable", shape = box3d, fillcolor = "#ffffff",
            color = "#666666"];
        L2 [label = "Dose / intervention input", shape = invhouse,
            fillcolor = "#ffffff", color = "#666666"];
        L3 [label = "Derived result of the model", shape = doubleoctagon,
            fillcolor = "#f0c03c", color = "#8a6a10"];
        L4 [label = "Measured clinical endpoint", shape = ellipse,
            fillcolor = "#f8d8d8", color = "#a84949"];
        L5 [label = "Closed-form note / anchor", shape = note,
            fillcolor = "#fff2c9", color = "#b08a20"];
        L6 [label = "activation →   inhibition ⊣\nred = the destructive loop\ngreen = the protective term",
            shape = plaintext, fillcolor = "#fafafa"];
        L1 -> L2 -> L3 -> L4 -> L5 -> L6 [style = invis];
    }
}
